  data:  # 825b
    kind: work_item  # 825b
    title: "dart constructors are identified by neither kind nor a fixed name, so construction reachability (INV-rolok) does not cover dart"  # 825b
    status: todo_hard  # 825b
    priority: 3  # 825b
    parent:  # 825b
    tags:  # 825b
    - analyzer  # 825b
    - dead_code  # 825b
    isbefore: []  # 825b
    duplicate_of: []  # 825b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 825b
    pr_ref:  # 825b
    description: "Filed from the INV-rolok fix rather than guessed at.\n\nsymbol_kinds.is_initializer identifies the code that runs on construction by\ntwo mechanisms: kind == \"constructor\" (java, csharp, apex, pony) or a\nper-language reserved NAME (python __init__, js/ts constructor, ruby\ninitialize, php __construct). Dart fits NEITHER: its constructors are named\nafter their class (Widget.Widget) and it also has named constructors\n(Widget.named, Widget.fromJson), so no fixed name table can identify them, and\ndart.py does not emit kind=\"constructor\".\n\nConsequence: dart is the one language named in INV-rolok's root_cause\n(py/dart/js_ts all point instantiates at the class) that the fix does NOT\ncover. A dart class reached only by construction still has its constructor and\neverything downstream reported as dead.\n\nTwo candidate directions:\n  A. dart.py emits kind=\"constructor\" for constructor declarations, which is\n     the canonical registry mechanism and makes is_initializer work with no\n     table entry. Check the blast radius on consumers keyed on kind==\"method\"\n     first -- note that kind=\"constructor\" also removes the symbol from\n     cli.production_callables, so dart constructors would stop being dead-code\n     candidates at all, which is a SEPARATE behavior change and may not be\n     wanted.\n  B. is_initializer compares the member's short name to its OWNER's short name\n     (member_owner), which identifies Widget.Widget without a table but does\n     not identify named constructors.\n\nUNMEASURED, deliberately: no dart repo was surveyed for this. Size it before\npicking. The item exists so the gap is a filed absence rather than a silent one\n-- the same reason the gap is written into _INITIALIZER_NAMES_BY_LANGUAGE's own\ncomment."  # 825b
    fields: {}  # 825b
- op: discuss  # 8edd
  at: '2026-11-01T10:56:04Z'  # 8edd
  by: agent  # 8edd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8edd
  clock: 2  # 8edd
  nonce: 8edd  # 8edd
  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/graph1/). VERDICT: MIS-PREMISED. Reviewed 2026-11-01 at dev 100b6fbb6e: dart.py DOES emit kind constructor (Widget.Widget, Widget.Widget.named; since 55296f5440), so is_initializer already returns True and options A/B are moot. The consequence still reproduces for other reasons: setup() called in a constructor body gets no edge (dart.py:827 function_scopes excludes constructors) and dead-code-maybe flags setup/helper; var w = Widget(1) without new emits no instantiates edge at all. MECHANISM: dart.py function_scopes maps only function/method kinds, so constructor-body calls have no caller; implicit ClassName(...) construction is not read."  # 8edd
